# Backend

Protected routers mount `requireAuth`, `requireTenant`, and `apiRateLimiter` before handlers. Register static paths before `/:id`.

```ts
router.use(requireAuth, requireTenant, apiRateLimiter);
router.post("/bulk", requireStaff, bulkSend); // before "/:id"
router.get("/:id", getEmail);
```

## Data access

- Read `userId` and `organizationId` from `req.auth`, set by `middleware/auth.ts`.
- Filter Supabase queries with `.eq("organizationId", req.auth.organizationId)` (and owner checks where the row is user-scoped).
- Throw `ApiError` (or `AuthorizationError`) and pass it to `next`. Do not send ad-hoc error JSON from controllers.
- Validate request bodies with zod before writing. Do not pass `req.body` straight into an update.

## AI and side effects

- AI calls go through the service layer, then `auditService` and `analyticsService`.
- Realtime emits use the org room: `org:${organizationId}`.
- Attachment bytes stay in Supabase Storage. The API only mints signed URLs and must restrict paths to the caller's `organizationId` prefix.
